/T (Universal outlook refers to an appreciation, sensitivity and commitment to universal issues. Ancient Indians viewed the world in holistic way, where every being, from the unicellular organism to man, has its own sacred place of pride. After years of mindless spillage of nature, the world needs to come to this universal view of life. The universal outlook helps the child view himself / herself as a responsible citizen of the world \(including world issues\), live in harmony with creative environment \(including education and synthesis between science and religion\) as well as become aware of being an intrinsic part of the macrocosm.)
/E (Universal outlook refers to an appreciation, sensitivity and commitment to universal issues. Ancient Indians viewed the world in holistic way, where every being, from the unicellular organism to man, has its own sacred place of pride. After years of mindless spillage of nature, the world needs to come to this universal view of life. The universal outlook helps the child view himself / herself as a responsible citizen of the world \(including world issues\), live in harmony with creative environment \(including education and synthesis between science and religion\) as well as become aware of being an intrinsic part of the macrocosm.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [1]
